{:edb/db-before-t 2725 :edb/db-after-t 2726 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536038 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:24:33.372Z" 13194139536038 true] [17592186129144 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380468 13194139536038 true] [17592186129147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380482 13194139536038 true] [17592186129208 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380491 13194139536038 true] [17592186198291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380477 13194139536038 true] [17592186198333 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380474 13194139536038 true] [17592186198334 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380471 13194139536038 true] [17592186198342 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380488 13194139536038 true] [17592186198344 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380485 13194139536038 true] [17592186380468 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380469 13194139536038 true] [17592186380468 1089 "q-169099" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380468 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536038 true] [17592186380468 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380468 1113 #uuid "a67886c7-3468-53c0-8e99-d5012cd7aa19" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380468 1145 "The mass $M$ of a plate that occupies the region \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nwith mass density $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nM={∬}_{D}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =[3{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the plate is $M=24.$" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380469 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380470 13194139536038 true] [17592186380469 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536038 true] [17592186380469 1041 "field-1" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380469 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380470 13194139536038 true] [17592186380469 1110 #uuid "501e9194-65b8-5a25-b0b4-5cc1454659c0" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380470 1034 "24" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380470 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536038 true] [17592186380470 1111 #uuid "054a9e46-29f6-5e90-a9fc-37fdcedfa68e" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380471 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380472 13194139536038 true] [17592186380471 1089 "q-169100" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380471 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536038 true] [17592186380471 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380471 1113 #uuid "46a2b42c-7958-5741-b473-35d19b9b5085" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380471 1145 "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ and the plate occupies the region\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}{[{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(2)^{4}-0 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380472 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380473 13194139536038 true] [17592186380472 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536038 true] [17592186380472 1041 "field-1" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380472 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380473 13194139536038 true] [17592186380472 1110 #uuid "50101599-38b0-5952-aec2-aaa66db8bcaa" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380473 1034 "36" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380473 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536038 true] [17592186380473 1111 #uuid "d183984c-4316-5da1-889c-062e0100ea7b" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380474 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380475 13194139536038 true] [17592186380474 1089 "q-169101" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380474 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536038 true] [17592186380474 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                    