                               \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380477 1113 #uuid "f09d23db-1982-5ecb-a0dc-09360906a070" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380477 1145 "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{M},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{M}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n* $M={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n* ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n* ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nIn part 1, we found that the mass of the plate is\n\n$$\nM=24.\n$$\n\nAlso, from parts 2 and 3, we know that \n\n$$\n{M}_{x}=36,\\,{M}_{y}=48.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{M}=\\frac{48}{24}=2,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{M}=\\frac{36}{24}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of mass of the lamina is $(2,\\frac{3}{2}).$" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380478 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380479 13194139536038 true] [17592186380478 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536038 true] [17592186380478 1041 "field-1" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380478 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380479 13194139536038 true] [17592186380478 1110 #uuid "942c8cf7-2fe0-522e-8d35-64ef961c3aff" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380479 1034 "2" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536038 true] [17592186380479 1111 #uuid "255dfde8-adfa-5aaa-807d-05d2819a1b54" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380480 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380481 13194139536038 true] [17592186380480 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536038 true] [17592186380480 1041 "field-2" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380480 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380481 131941395360