egin{aligned}{I}_{s} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}(y-2)^{2}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{4}-4{y}^{3}+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{[\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}-{y}^{4}+\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =9[\\frac{32}{5}-16+\\frac{32}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380489 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380490 13194139536038 true] [17592186380489 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536038 true] [17592186380489 1041 "field-1" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380489 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380490 13194139536038 true] [17592186380489 1110 #uuid "a63e90b3-4ec6-5c39-9e52-691aa4b08d81" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380490 1034 "\\frac{48}{5}" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380490 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536038 true] [17592186380490 1111 #uuid "b122c958-e497-565e-a75d-39b1575adf0e" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380491 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380492 13194139536038 true] [17592186380491 1089 "q-169106" 13194139536038 true] [17592186380491 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536038 true] [17592186380491 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n    